# Ordinary least squares line fit, y = a + b x (n = 40)

## Data and method
The 40 points in `/initial-state/inputs/0/points.csv` (sha256 `5eec9bbc34f6996cd84748d85e95d9114bd263ff6bafda0cfcda8aa80a5c2905`; x = 0 to 9.75 in steps of 0.25) were fitted by ordinary least squares, y = a + b x. Confidence intervals use Student's t with n - 2 = 38 degrees of freedom (t = 2.0244). The residual standard deviation is s = sqrt(RSS / (n - 2)). The data's provenance and units are not given, so none are assumed.

## Results
All values are from `results/ols_results.json`, produced by the code below.

| Quantity | Estimate | Std. error | 95% CI |
|---|---|---|---|
| a (intercept) | 1.4840 | 0.1453 | [1.1898, 1.7781] |
| b (slope) | 0.8303 | 0.0257 | [0.7784, 0.8822] |

- Residual SD: s = 0.4682 (38 dof).
- R² = 0.965.
- The fit matches `scipy.stats.linregress` (intercept, slope and both standard errors).
- Residual diagnostics show no sign of non-normality (Shapiro-Wilk p = 0.40) or lag-1 autocorrelation (Durbin-Watson = 1.91).

The fitted line is y = 1.484 + 0.830 x. The slope interval excludes 0, and the intercept interval excludes 0 as well.

